      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In this initial study, we found that autoantibodies against actin and myosin were present during and after an acute coronary syndrome. Moreover, they correlated with persistent troponin-I elevation at follow-up, and with late myocardial infarction."},
